 # Changelog
 
+## [v0.1.39-test.1] - 2026-11-26
+
+> R52 bounded receiver-store readiness. This closes a cold-start race that could disable receiver-scoped experiment memory on the first Bluetooth attempt; it does not claim to fix the E2LB vehicle connection.
+
+### English
+- Start loading the private receiver configuration store from `Application.onCreate`, not only after the session controller is first ensured.
+- Publish store readiness exactly once after both the persisted HMAC secret and environment fingerprint have loaded successfully (or initialization has failed).
+- Bluetooth session workers may wait up to 1.5 seconds for readiness before creating a receiver observation; timeout/failure proceeds without a binding and never blocks indefinitely.
+- Preserve receiver identity isolation: no empty-binding or raw-address fallback key is introduced.
+- Add concurrent waiter, initialization-failure, timeout, interruption-preservation and one-shot completion tests.
+- Full Android Gradle build and E2LB real-vehicle behavior remain unverified.
+
+### 简体中文
+- 将本机接收端配置存储初始化提前到 `Application.onCreate`，不再只依赖会话控制器首次初始化。
+- 只有持久化 HMAC 密钥和环境指纹均加载完成（或明确初始化失败）后，才一次性发布存储就绪状态。
+- 蓝牙会话工作线程在创建车机观察对象前最多等待 1.5 秒；超时或失败时安全地不使用持久化绑定，不会无限阻塞连接。
+- 保留按车机隔离原则，不引入空绑定或原始地址回退键。
+- 新增并发等待、初始化失败、超时、中断状态保留和一次性完成测试。
+- 完整 Android 编译与 E2LB 实车行为仍未验证。
+
 ## [v0.1.38-test.1] - 2026-11-26
 
 > R51 receiver-scoped E2LB fallback isolation. This prevents missing receiver bindings from sharing persistent A/B state; it does not claim to fix the E2LB vehicle connection.
